     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "As effective as sulfonylureas and metformin in lowering A1C. W biopsy-proven MASH or ↑risk of liver fibrosis, a GLP-1 RA = preferred; pioglitazone can be considered for its potential benefit on MASH. Needs endogenous insulin: ⍉for type 1 DM or DKA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Pioglitazone 15 or 30 mg PO daily (15 mg w NYHA I–II HF); titrate by 15 mg to max 45 mg daily. Max 15 mg w gemfibrozil or other strong CYP2C8 inhibitors."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " → or worsens CHF in some pts; ⍉recommended in Sxtomatic HF; starting it in NYHA class III–IV HF = contraindicated. Pioglitazone: don't use w active bladder CA; caution w prior bladder CA, edema, or liver dz."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fluid retention/periph edema (most w insulin) and wt gain, sometimes > 10 kg; can worsen HF. Fractures (more in women), macular edema. Pioglitazone: poss bladder CA (data conflicting). Rosiglitazone: may raise risk of HF, angina, MI, CVA. Hypoglycemia mainly when combined w insulin or a sulfonylurea."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Gemfibrozil (strong CYP2C8 inhibitor) raises pioglitazone exposure about 3-fold. W insulin, cut the insulin dose 10–25% if hypoglycemia occurs."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pioglitazone:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " liver tests b4 starting; routine periodic LFTs ⍉needed w.o liver dz. Check LFTs promptly for Sx of liver inj; stop if ALT > 3× ULN. After starting or raising the dose, watch for wt gain, edema and HF signs. Regular eye exams."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Can promote wt gain; use judiciously @ the lowest dose in people w obesity."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
